    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`). Here's what I implemented and why it keeps structural impact low.\n\n## Change summary\n\nThe postcode feature is added as **small, self-contained units** rather than by growing any existing function:\n\n**New, cohesive units (each tiny, zero surrounding complexity):**\n- `RejectInvalidPostcode` \u2014 one pipeline step: skips when postcode absent, rejects a non-4-digit value, then rejects a 4-digit value outside its region's range. Region comes from the existing `Locality.of(city)` helper (Sydney\u2192NSW, etc.); an unknown region accepts any 4-digit value.\n- `InvalidPostcodeException` + `InvalidPostcodeExceptionHandler` + its escalation YAML \u2014 a dedicated checked-exception \u2192 400 route, mirroring the existing `CrowdedCity`/`NotFound` pattern.\n- Wired the new step into `owners.POST.yml` after `rejectDailyLimit`, before `build`.\n\n**Minimal edits to existing files (no complexity growth):**\n- `Owner.java` \u2014 added a `postcode` field with a plain getter/setter and `@Column` (storage). MapStruct auto-maps it both directions by name, so `OwnerMapper` needed no change.\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added the optional `postcode` property (4-digit pattern) to `OwnerFields`, so the generated DTO carries it and it's returned in the `Owner` response; it's not in `required`, keeping the request contract backward-compatible.\n- `db/hsqldb/schema.sql` + `data.sql` \u2014 added the column (at the end) and padded the positional seed inserts, since the test profile runs `ddl-auto=none` against this schema.\n\n## Behavior vs. spec\n- Valid postcode \u2192 stored and returned (`coreStoresValidPostcode` \u2705).\n- Absent postcode \u2192 accepted (`coreAcceptsOwnerWithoutPostcode` \u2705).\n- Malformed / out-of-range postcode \u2192 400 (`errorRejectsMalformedPostcode` \u2705).\n\nOne implementation note: `@Valid` on the DTO's `pattern` isn't enforced at the `@Val` variable hand-off (only at `@RequestBody` binding), so the format check lives in `RejectInvalidPostcode` alongside the range check \u2014 one place, one exception, guaranteed 400. The full suite is green.",
